course: dictionary
lesson: 5100
title: Words that come and go
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The words around a new word are its context, and they often give clues. «Sniffs were frequent and sobs only intermittent» sets two things side by side: the sniffs kept going, but the sobs came and went. So intermittent must mean coming now and then.
explain: Intermittent means stopping and starting again and again, so it is not continuous. Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. The sobs came, stopped, came again: that fits, so your meaning is right.
explain: You will meet this word about weather and machines too. Intermittent rain falls, stops, then falls again. An intermittent signal works, drops out, then works again. The clue to look for is the pattern of stopping and starting again.
fact: Intermittent means stopping and starting again and again; it is not continuous.
fact: «Intermittent» means coming now and then, not all the time.
fact: Intermittent rain, intermittent showers and an intermittent signal all come and go.
fact: Continuous means carrying on without a break, so it is the opposite of intermittent.
fact: Context clues, like the words that sit beside a new word, can help you work out its meaning.
exercise: «Sniffs were frequent and sobs only intermittent.» What does intermittent mean here? | Very loud | Never stopping at all | Happy and bright | *Coming now and then
exercise: The forecast says «intermittent showers» this afternoon. What should you expect? | No rain at all | *Rain that comes and goes | Rain that never stops | Snow on the hills
exercise: Which word means the opposite of intermittent? | Quiet | Broken | Sometimes | *Continuous
test: The wifi signal was intermittent, so the video froze and then played again. What does intermittent mean? | Very fast | Not working at all, ever | *Stopping and starting again and again | Strong and steady all day
test: An intermittent fault is one that | always stays the same | makes a very loud noise | never works at all | *works, fails, then works again
exam: Jayden says a machine has an intermittent fault. Which description is right? | It keeps running without a break | It has never worked | *It stops and starts again and again | It is very loud
